In article <30DAC4BB.7D6B@csi.nb.ca>
Andrew Grant <agrant@csi.nb.ca> wrote:

> Does anyone know the procedure for setting up quotas on a DEC
> OSF1 machine.  I know about the quota, vquotaon programs, but they keep 
> talking about a certain file system in the fstab needs to be configured.
> Also what is the format of the quota.user and quota.group files since I 
> can't seem to find them (ie. How do I create them)

I don't have a manual in front of me, but these are the important ones:

a) Make sure that "options QUOTA" is in your options file, and that vmunix is built with it.

b) Verify QUOTA_CONFIG=yes in /etc/rc/config (set with rcmgr).
fenster@hostname> rcmgr get QUOTA_CONFIG
yes

c) Verify that quotas are enabled for the file systems in /etc/fstab (see man fstab)

For example:
/dev/rz2d        /var   ufs rw,userquota 1 2
/dev/rz2f        swap1  ufs sw 0 2
/dev/rz6c       /cdrom  ufs     ro      0 0
domain_rz3a#old_root    /old_root       advfs rq,userquota,groupquota   0 2

> 
> Thanks
> --Andrew

