organization: CS Dept., Umass-Amherst
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.sys.dec,gnu.gcc.help

Marc Goldburg (marcg@alphonse.arraycomm.com) wrote:

: When linking gcc2.7.2-compiled objects on a Digital Unix 3.2c, the following
: warnings appear

: /usr/bin/ld:
: Warning: Linking some objects which contain exception information sections
:         and some which do not. This may cause fatal runtime exception handling
:         problems (last obj encountered without exceptions was version.o).

You might install GNU AS on your system. The installation of binutils
installs a copy of GNU AS under, according to your configure,
/usr/local/gnu/alpha-dec-osf3.2/bin. If you remove this copy, gcc
will not use it. It is fine with /bin/as. That is why it is not show
up on during stage1 compilation.

This copy of AS affects the current installation of gcc as well.

: gcc is configured as follows

:         ./configure --build=alpha-dec-osf3.2 --prefix=/usr/local/gnu

: The precise OS versions are

:         Digital UNIX V3.2C  (Rev. 148); Fri Oct 27 19:48:58 PDT 1995 
:         Digital UNIX V3.2C Worksystem Software (Rev. 148)

: Proper exception handling, esp. for floating point exceptions, is important
: in many of our applications.  Is there a fix available?

: Thanks in advance,

: Marc Goldburg

: P.S. these errors can be seen during the build of the stage 2 gcc itself,
: for example

: stage1/xgcc -Bstage1/  -DIN_GCC   -g -O2   -o collect2 collect2.o  cplus-dem.o u
: nderscore.o version.o obstack.o ` case "stage1/xgcc -Bstage1/" in "cc") echo "" 
: ;; esac `  -lmld
: /usr/bin/ld:
: Warning: Linking some objects which contain exception information sections
:         and some which do not. This may cause fatal runtime exception handling
:         problems (last obj encountered without exceptions was version.o).
