In article <4bvl3n$2b1@news.service.uci.edu>
iglesias@draco.acs.uci.edu (Mike Iglesias) writes:
iglesias> This patch is supposed to fix the problem.  Rebuild gcc
iglesias> after applying the patch.
[...]
iglesias> ! #define ASM_SPEC "-g3 -nocpp %{pg}"
  
This patch was the workaround for the mips-tfile problem on 3.2c with
gcc prior to 2.7.2.  A slightly more elaborate version of this patch
was incorporated into 2.7.2 so it is now obsolete, and certainly won't
fix the linker warnings.

You can suppress the linker warning by adding the undocumented flag
'-no_excpt' to the link specs, but this turns out to be a bad idea as
some third party products depend on exceptions working properly.

As far as I know the warning is harmless and the only cure I know of
isn't, so currently we just live with the warning message.
