Paul Mitchell (mitchell@envy.ph.ed.ac.uk) wrote:
: I'm trying to configure a OSF V3.2 system to act as a slave NIS server -
: this all works fine, but the problem I have is that there are SunOS 4.1
: boxes in my subnet, that seem to require their NIS master to forward
: non-local host loookup to DNS (named on a Solaris machine).  SunOS doesn't
: have an /etc/nsswitch.conf or /etc/svc.conf and therefore expects the NIS
: master to take care of this.  So when my SunOS machines bind to the OSF
: machine as an NIS server, they break.

As I understand it, no vendor other than Sun has ever supported this
NIS to DNS forwarding.  At one time, my favorite solution was to
recompile libc on SunOS 4.x so that name lookups went directly to DNS,
causing NIS host maps to be bypassed-- no NIS query, no chance to hang
yourself.

If you go this route, be careful about replacing dynamic libraries
while the system is running....

I didn't do this myself, so I don't know where are the appropriate
sources/binaries.  I suggest asking Sun.

