(J Frankland) writes: 
>
>The threads programming example in the Guide to DECthreads (accessible
>by the bookreader) which conducts a prime number search, crashes.
>It is Example 5-1.  After compiling with the -lpthreads link flag, and
>running it, it Seg Faults before it get to the main() function.

On 3.2c, we traced this problem to the DEC shared libraries pulled in
by -lpthreads.

In our other words, even the simple program below would seg fault:
***********

main()
{
    printf("Hello world\n");
    exit(0);
}
******************
It doesn't even have any thread calls!

We were able to run thread applications after manually linking in the
other libraries.



