running on your system and then put Advfs on top of it to get true
striping.  Or get a RAID controller for the system and let it do the work.

Randy> 3) My application (GIANT POP mail server) does a huge amount of writes
Randy>    (small files < 2K in size). Is there anything I can do to optimize
Randy>    ADVFS write?

You could get a Prestoserve NVRAM board.  DEC has 1, 4 and 8MB
versions for the PCI bus; 1, 2 and 4MB versions for EISA.  

What I would do is get monitor from gatekeeper.dec.com and see how
loaded your system is, and where the bottleneck is.  For example, do
you have too little memory and the system is swapping alot?  Is CPU
utilization high or low?  How busy are the disks?  And so on.  99,000
access a day is only 68.75 accesses per minute on average, though I'm
sure the peak is higher than that at times.  

