you probably had the default settings when creating advfs volume, there is lack of
space for "i-nodes"-like allocation units in advfs by default.

> Recently, I added a second RZ28 to the spool (I really, really love
> addvol) and I've been able to bring expirations back up to 5 days,
> and DF reports that the fileset is only 55% full.
i had the same problem...

> this for some time, but they've been unable to respond promptly and
> appropriate to panics, and security issues, so I just threw up my
> hands and forgot about it.
;)
usual thing with DEC support ;)

so here is the solution:

1. backup your current news spool advfs volume, but don't use vdump - it's awful ;)
use tar or better gtar.
2. use mkfdmn command to create new domain (overwrite current rather) like:
mkfdmn -o -x <value> /dev/rzxx domain_name.
-x is the undocumented in manual pages option.
You can find the description in Release Notes for OSF 3.2 and probably later releases.
this option allows to change the default value of space for small files.
There is a table showing what must be the value for predefined number of files.
3. tune rw blocks (you can do that on the fly), try as bigger as possible, that
increases performance.

that's all.
i'm using advfs for uucp and news spool w/o any problem after these manipulations.
i have about 200000 news files...

