Andrew Grant (agrant@csi.nb.ca) wrote:
: Does anyone know the procedure for setting up quotas on a DEC
: OSF1 machine.  I know about the quota, vquotaon programs, but they keep 
: talking about a certain file system in the fstab needs to be configured.
: Also what is the format of the quota.user and quota.group files since I 
: can't seem to find them (ie. How do I create them)

First the easy one.  You don't create the quota.user quota.group
files.  They are created for you went you set up the quotas.  

I'm not sure what message you are getting, but your filesystem entry
in fstab should look something like,

users#user00   /user00  advfs  rq,userquota,groupquota

Sorry, all my quotas are on Advfs filesystems.  The one thing that may
not be obvious from the man pages is that userquota and groupquota are
required if you're going to have quotas.  The man pages seem to imply
that they're needed only if you want to put the quota.user and
quota.group files someplace unexpected.

