In article <4ak145$7t4@news.res.ray.com>, tringali@news.ed.ray.com (Scott Tringali) writes:
|>How do I create my own shared libraries?  I am working with a large (30+)
|>number of applications that have many common libraries.  These are created with
|>cc -c, then ar, and then linked into the final application with cc.
|>
|>Is there any way I can take these libraries, compile them to a .so, and save on
|>disk space and memory?  I haven't found any references how to do this in the cc
|>or ld man pages.
|>

You didn't look hard enough.  It is in the ld(1) manual page:

NAME

  ld, uld - link editor	and ucode link editor

SYNOPSIS

  ld [ option ... ] file ...
  uld [	option ... ] file ...

DESCRIPTION

  The ld command invokes the DEC OSF/1 link editor which links extended	coff
  object files.	 The archive format understood by ld is	the one	created	by
  the archiver ar(1).

  -shared
      Produce a	shared object.	This includes creating all of the tables for
      run-time linking and resolving references	to other specified shared
      objects.	The object created may be used by the linker to	make dynamic
      executables.

  -call_shared
      Produce a	dynamic	executable.  The object	created	may use	shared
      objects at run-time.


Here is a simple example.  Note that LD_LIBRARY_PATH must be set to include
the directory with the shared library, or, the library must live in
/usr/shlib.

scratch> cat Makefile
all:	sharedapp

sharedapp:	main.o shlib.so
	cc -call_shared -o sharedapp main.o shlib.so

main.o:	main.c
	cc -g -c main.c

shlib.so:	shlib.o
	ld -shared shlib.o -o shlib.so /usr/shlib/libc.so

shlib.o:	shlib.c
	cc -g -c shlib.c

clean:
	rm -f sharedapp main.o shlib.so 

scratch> cat main.c
#include <stdio.h>

void main()
{
    void sharedRoutine(void);

    printf("In the main program.\n");
    sharedRoutine();
}

scratch> cat shlib.c
#include <stdio.h>

void sharedRoutine(void)
{
    printf("In the shared routine in the shared library.\n");
}

scratch> make clean all
rm -f sharedapp main.o shlib.so 
cc -g -c main.c
ld -shared shlib.o -o shlib.so /usr/shlib/libc.so
cc -call_shared -o sharedapp main.o shlib.so
scratch> (export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=.; ./sharedapp)
In the main program.
In the shared routine in the shared library.
scratch> (export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=.; ladebug ./sharedapp)
