You can run a cluster of Digital Unix machines in diskless mode which
means that they boot from the main-server and the mount all filesystem via
NFS from the file-server. They still can have local disks for swapping and
tmp-space though. Each machine still has a (small to medium) private part
on the server for setup-files and machine-dependant binaries.

I don't know anything about OpenVMS cluster, so it can be that I don't
answer your question.

