> 
>get the description of your disk (a small paper delivered with) and
>write a simillar disktab entry witha new name (ST12400 etc..).
>IT's easy and I had no problems at all.

This is not a good way to do it. In many cases you will not be able to access
all of the disk space.

The proper way to do this is to use disklabel(8). It can ask the drive for its
configuration and write the appropriate label. Hand editing disktab for SCSI
drives is probably never a good idea. If you know the rotational speed of the
disk, you might want to correct that value as the current version of
disklabel(8) always assumes 3600 RPM, but it's generally not significant due to
the SCSI controller doing most of the optimization.

