In article <DJsv93.9Fo@txnews.amd.com>, clive@dvorak.amd.com (Clive Dawson) writes:
>I'm receiving messages of the following form on my AlphaStation 600
>running Digital UNIX V3.2C:
>
>	vmunix: fork/procdup: task_create failed. Code: 0x11
>
>Can anybody give me some details on what this means?  In particular,
>does the code indicate a particular resource is lacking?


That 0x11 is KERN_LIMIT_EXCEEDED in the <include/mach/kern_return.h>.
Most likely, you ran up against your per-user process limit -- maxuprc.
You can up this value in /etc/sysconfigtab.





