>I have found all the other libraries mentioned(cob,curses,...) but not the
>sort library.  Has anyone dealt with this problem before or got any ideas?
>
>						hugh@du.edu

You need to install the sort runtime library - it's in it's own subset.  
The sort library subset is not installed by default as part of the OS 
install, but it is shipped on the OS disk.  Look for a subset with the title 
of 'Sort Runtime Library' - the actual subset name is SORLIBXXX.

