In article <4b1g3p$bq7@fu-berlin.de> pleiter@titania.physik.fu-berlin.de (Dirk Pleiter) writes:

> The conf.h turns out not to be correct for OSF/1 (or dUNIX).
> I had to add the following two lines:
> 
> # define _PATH_VENDOR_CF	"/var/adm/sendmail/sendmail.cf"
> # define USE_VENDOR_CF_PATH
> 
> to the "OSF/1 (tested on Alpha)" section of conf.h (see below for
> the conf.h I used).

What exactly is the point of teaching 8.7.x where to look for
sendmail.cf on various platforms? Why not pick a single standard
directory...like /etc...and stick with it? It seems kind of silly to
have to hunt around for the sendmail.cf, and it's not like you want to
install sendmail 8 and have it start using whatever vendor config file
happens to be sitting there.

One of the reaasons we use sendmail 8 is to simplify sendmail
administration in a heterogeneous network. It doesn't make sense to go
out of our way to customize the installation to conform with each
vendor's whims.

