: Hello,

: our lab considers buying an external CD-ROM writer to store our huge
: digital image data. We plan to read the data on DEC Alphas with OSF3.0/3.2
: or on Pentium PC/Linux. 

: Can the Alphas read the (presumably) ISO9660 CD-ROMs? And if not, what can
: we do instead?

Yes it can, but when you build your kernel you need to make sure that
you have an option that looks like:

options         CDFS

in your kernel config file.


: Also, can the Alpha's CD-ROM drives play ordinary music CDs? 
: The drive has an earphone jack and even volume control ;-)


Yes, but you need to have software, xcd or xmcd (which is my favorite,
look at http://www.omega.com/~ti/www/xmcd/ for more info) and a set of
external speakers or a set of headphones.  I have a pair of cheap
Labtec speakers connected to mine.


: Thanks,
: Petr


Your welcome,
Phillip



