Norman
	OSF does not need disktab entries.  Try this on your drive:

# disklabel -wr /dev/rrz0c /dev/rrz0c

This askes the device driver (to go ask the drive) for disk parameters
and writes them to the drive.  Use 'diskedit -e' to edit the table to
your liking.

-or-

# newfs /dev/rrz2c /dev/rrz2c

If you are only going to use the c partition.  You don't even need to
label it.  If your using ADVFS or lsm I would label it.

Andy.
