David Arnold (arnold@foxtail.dstc.edu.au) wrote:
: I'm trying to increase the number of threads allowed per user under
: Alpha OSF/1 3.2c.  Using /sbin/sysconfig & /etc/sysconfigtab to set
: the proc sub-system parameters, I tried setting the max processes to
: 1024 and max threads to 4096.

: However, after rebooting, the values obtained from `sysconfig -q proc`
: were 267 and 532 respectively.  

: Is this some hard limit?

I think the limit is the maximum number built into the kernel, I could 
decrease the values but not increase over the kernel limit.

: Is there some way to exceed these figures?

Edit /sys/conf/YOURHOSTNAMEHERE and modify/add 

maxuprc         1024        #Max processes per username

rebuild the kernel, mv them to / and reboot. 
The name of max_threads in the config file I don't know.

Juergen
 



