Dana Huggard (dana@tvinet.com) said:
: cc -Olimit 1000 -I. -O -I/usr/sww/include -DNDBM -DNEWDB -DNIS  -c map.c
: /usr/lib/cmplrs/cc/cfe: Error: map.c: 45: Cannot open file db.h for #include
: *** Exit 1
: Stop.
:  Can anyone enlighten me on "db.h"?
	Okay! I guess you didn't really read the READ_ME in the src directory!
:-) Anyway, here is what it says in READ_ME:

The three options are NEWDB (the new Berkeley DB package), NDBM (the
older DBM implementation -- the very old V7 implementation is no
longer supported), and NIS (Network Information Services).  Used alone
these just include the support they indicate.  [If you are using NEWDB,
get the latest version from FTP.CS.Berkeley.EDU in /ucb/4bsd/db.tar.Z
(or db.tar.gz).  DO NOT use the version from the Net2 distribution!

So go to get a copy of db.tar.gz, and after you compile it, put the
path of db.h into the src/Makefiles/Makefile.OSF1 like :

INCDIRS=-I/usr/sww/include -I/tmp/db.1.85/PORT/include
			   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
and
LIBDIRS=-L/usr/sww/lib -L/usr/shlib -L/usr/lib -L/tmp/db.1.85/PORT/osf.1.0.2
     					       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Of course, your path will not be the same as mine. By the way, in your db.h
,you might need to change the following line into:
#include <sys/cdefs.h>  to 
#include <cdefs.h>

Then, I successfully made my sendmail last night. Hope you too! Good Luck!
8-)

