In Article <30C315E0.41C6@golay.med.unc.edu>
"Gernot M. Fuchs" <gfuchs@golay.med.unc.edu> writes:
>oberman@icaen.llnl.gov wrote:
>
>> Netscape will grab almost all available color map slots if you don't override
>> this rude behavior.
>> 
>To get things strait: does this mean DEC does not support 'state of the art' 
>colour depths with their X-Servers even under dUNIX, resulting in severely
>restricted graphic capabilities?

No. Digital supports 24 bit true color if the hardware does and you set up the
system so that the X server knows it. The original post did not say that more
than standard, 8 bit video was available in the system. If it is not, you are
restricted to 256 colors, whether on a Sun, SGI, or Alpha. X11 does not
magically make added colors available on any system.

If you have a 24 bit card that is supported on the Alpha, you will get 24 bit
capabilities from X. the X server is not an issue here. Only the hardware and
the driver are!

