We have a user on our DEC 3000/600 (160M of memory, OSF/1 v2.0) who 
runs a large CFD (computational fluid dynamics) code that recently 
seems to take down the system every time.  The same code compiled and 
ran with the same parameters about three weeks ago with no problems.  
We've figured out that the program shouldn't be using more than about 
28M of array space.  There don't seem to be any messages in the log 
files saying that something was wrong just before the crash. 

Is it just a bug in v2.0 possibly?  Is there somewhere else I should
look?  Is it reasonable that a single user can take down the system
(sure doesn't seem like it to me)?

Any help or pointers where to look are appreciated (I already looked
through the FAQ and the on-line documentation to no avail).

