In article <ARNOLD.95Dec4103044@foxtail.dstc.edu.au> arnold@foxtail.dstc.edu.au (David Arnold) writes:

>   I'm trying to increase the number of threads allowed per user under
>   Alpha OSF/1 3.2c.  Using /sbin/sysconfig & /etc/sysconfigtab to set
>   the proc sub-system parameters, I tried setting the max processes to
>   1024 and max threads to 4096.
>
>   However, after rebooting, the values obtained from `sysconfig -q proc`
>   were 267 and 532 respectively.  
>
>   Is this some hard limit?
>   Is there some way to exceed these figures?

Sysconfig will let you increase these values until you hit a
'semi-hard' limit.  These limits can be increased by increasing
maxusers in the kernel configuration file and rebuilding the kernel.
I use:

maxusers        64

To set the limits you're shooting for, you may have to go a little
higher than 64 for maxusers -- sorry, I don't remember offhand what
the formula used is.

