organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
reply-to: denham@zk3.dec.com (Jeffrey M. Denham)
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


In article <DIvy76.5I6@ampex.com>, chungto@ampex.com (Tony Chung) writes:
>On page 2-84 of the  Writing Device Drivers: Reference
>	"You can enable this debugging feature at boot time by providing
>the boot parameter kmem_debug=1."
>
>The question is how?  Which file to insert this "kmem_debug=1"?
>
>Thanks for any help.
>---
>=============================
>Tony Chung
>chungto@ampex.com
>
>

Two ways to do this:

1. Boot time.

	>>>> boot -flags i

	Attempt the prompt type the kernel name and the paramter:

	vmunix kmem_debug=1

2. Use sysconfigtab. Add these lines to /etc/sysconfigtab:

   generic:
	kmem-debug = 1

The first approach is for one boot up only. The second will set kmem_debug
each time you boot.
-- 

