mark@chem.uwa.edu.au (Mark C Favas - SysAd) writes:

>I've just had a bunch of the following message pairs appear on the console
>and in the kern.log file written to by syslog:

>    Nov 30 11:01:21 gecko vmunix: svckudp_send: xdr_replymsg failed
>    Nov 30 11:01:21 gecko vmunix: rfs_dispatch: sendreply failed

> I've not seen this before - does anyone
>know what it means? Should I get worried?

There are a lot of random reasons for these.  Usually they mean the system is
low on memory or a route to the client went away.  Generally nothing to worry
about, as the client will simply retransmit the request and things will
keep going.

The message exists in part because NFS is fairly talkative - these messages
generally save more time diagnosing real problems than they waste as noise.

If they worry too many people we could retire some of the noisier messages.
