G'day,

Our site is looking at implementing DECAthena across our Digital
Unix(OSF/1) and Ultrix systems (approx. 80 hosts). Have people had any
experiences with this product, good and/or bad, that they could pass onto
me? 

We mainly need it for distributed user accounts and passwords, but the
extra management functionality looks very attractive. We have been running
Ultrix Enhanced Security (Kerberos) on 60+ DECstations, across 4 subnets
and a WAN, for the past 3 years. And are fairly comfortable with how it
all hangs together. We hope DECAthena will be a reasonably natural
progression of this arrangement (yes, I know Athena isn't a 'direct'
upgrade from ES, but it provides the same sort of tools, and more)... 

Email or posting to this newsgroup is fine. Thankyou for your time. 

